<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tmux on ByF (BaiFan) · Daily Deep Think</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/tmux/</link><description>Recent content in Tmux on ByF (BaiFan) · Daily Deep Think</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</managingEditor><webMaster>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</webMaster><copyright>CC BY-NC 4.0</copyright><lastBuildDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.baifan.site/en/tags/tmux/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>All the Tmux You'll Ever Use: Sessions, Panes, Detach</title><link>https://blog.baifan.site/en/tmux-practical-guide/</link><pubDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>blog@baifan.site (ByF (BaiFan))</author><guid>https://blog.baifan.site/en/tmux-practical-guide/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;You SSH into a server to run a long task, the network drops, and the task is gone. Tmux exists to solve exactly this — it decouples the terminal session from the window, so the process keeps running after you close the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- more --&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="my-6 flex flex-col items-center"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://blog.baifan.site/pictures/posts/tmux-session-window-pane.svg" alt="Tmux session-window-pane structure diagram" style="max-width: 800px;" class="rounded-lg shadow-md mx-auto center" loading="lazy" /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 italic"&gt;Tmux&amp;#39;s three layers: a Session contains Windows, a Window contains Panes&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;The Core Problem It Solves&#10; &lt;div id="the-core-problem-it-solves" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#the-core-problem-it-solves" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An ordinary terminal window is bound to its processes. Close the window and the processes die. Same story when SSH drops.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>